ens in the Shogunate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. DB2e doesn't actually state that it was definitively, only that they have claims of it, and that they might be true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T07:21:03-07:00","id":486343,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the references. I'll go read up on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T21:40:06-07:00","id":492315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/481501-legendary-and-dead-dragon-blooded?p=482177#post482177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nono, Primordial Principle Emulation was in Glories of the Most High; K'Tula had been referenced in Lands of Creation somewhere in the write-up about the West*, including the whole &quot;octopus body&quot; thing and how she was trying to create a new race of humanity, and Nephilpal used her as the jumping off point for the Charm by introducing the premise that she couldn't develop Solar Charms to make use of her new form.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found her reference in Lands of Creation page 124 (Grotto of Light) but I didn't find the one I was thinking about, where she was mentioned in some Artifact writeup or another. I also never found Primordial Principle Emulation in Lords of Creation or in the Scroll of Errata or in the Ink Monkeys collection - where is that? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arian Dynas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/481501-legendary-and-dead-dragon-blooded?p=485606#post485606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has EVERYONE forgot General Nefavarin? Leader of the 7th Legion? Founder of Lookshy? VERY, VERY dead?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have forgotten him, what's the reference again, Outcase or something? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/481501-legendary-and-dead-dragon-blooded?p=485701#post485701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will go you one better, has everyone forgotten that the shogunate was actually ruled over by a terrestrial shogun? The bloodline of which may or may not still be kicking around. Forgetting about that is kind of on par with forgetting about MRL or the Scarlet Empress.</div> </div> </div> </div>Raikuru's Dream, page 98 Ink Monkeys Ultimate? He's in stasis, I wouldn't go so far as to say he's dead. And nobody seems to remember him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T21:56:47-07:00","id":492331,"title":"","content":"Raikuru only <b><i>believes</i></b> he's the heir to the Shogunate. The Ink Monkeys didn't say he actually <b><i>is</i></b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T23:19:22-07:00","id":492374,"title":"","content":"Presumably the Shoguns had tons of kids, and there were various coups, usurpations, bastards, etc, so there's probably multiple DBs who have a claim to be heir to the Shogunate, if they had the geneological records to prove it.<br /> I think it's a reasonable thing to have DBs interact with in a game. In the DB game I played, one guy was told by some gods he was the heir to the Shogunate, for example (though I think those gods made it up). In my own game, the celestial players once came across some Lookshy archeologists who were trying to find records as to who is the heir to the Shogunate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T00:53:20-07:00","id":492410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also never found Primordial Principle Emulation in Lords of Creation or in the Scroll of Errata or in the Ink Monkeys collection - where is that?</div> </div> </div> </div> I... say where it is in the very first sentence of what you quoted of me... <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raikuru only believes he's the heir to the Shogunate. The Ink Monkeys didn't say he actually is.</div> </div> </div> </div> I read that as being akin to how most Chinese dynasties didn't practice strict primogeniture, or even directly codify succession process at all, so the heir of an emperor was either whomever they designated or whomever could drum up enough support for the interpretation that they had been designated. In other words, there's never any clear demarcation between somebody believing that they're an heir and somebody actually being such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T02:09:05-07:00","id":492444,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I explained Primogeniture to some Chinese friends and they were a bit surprised by how simple and cast-iron it was, and how Harry just has to accept he isn't going to be King (not, I think, that he wants to be).<br /> <br /> The Chinese system varied by dynasty, and even within dynasty. One, I recall, used a system whereby the Emperor and someone else (maybe the Chief Eunuch?) would both have the name of the successor sealed in a special box. When the Emperor died, if both boxes had the same name in, that Prince would be the new Emperor. If they had different names, both of the two named princes would be executed.<br /> I can see that getting messy.<br /> It also got complicated because of multiple wives, concubines, etc. Wives were always scheming to become Empress to raise the status of their son.<br /> <br /> Since the Shogunate was supposed to have been wracked by civil war, I'd imagine that either an informal or convulated system seems likely, since simple, formal systems generally lead to a more peaceful transition (if not necessarily to very good rulers).<br /> Also, with the added complication of Exaltation, it'd likely need to be more complicated. Presumably, only Dragonblood could become Shogun. What if the Shogun doesn't have any Dragonblooded children? What about how many DB children each of the Shogun's child has?<br /> What if the children are a different aspect to the Shogun, is that seen as a problem?<br /> What if one child is younger, but has much better breeding (because they have a different other parent)?<br /> Are the children of a mortal consort as likely to inherit as those born of a purely Dragonblood union?<br /> Does gender matter? Do younger children get large tracts of land when the Shogun died?<br /> What if a younger child inherits because they're a Dragonblood and the older one isn't, but then after the coronation the older child exalts?<br /> Then there's the fact that by the time of the Shogun's death (since they could live for a couple of hundred years if they don't get assassinated)* they might have a ton of kids, grandkids, etc. So an elder DB son with no DB kids or grandkids might be less acceptable than a younger daughter with 5 DB kids.<br /> What about religion? England has had a peaceful succession between Kings (not counting Protectors of the Realm) from Henry VII in 1485 up to today, with one exception; James II. He fell afoul of the &quot;no Catholics allowed&quot; rule and was overthrown in favour of his daughter (he then ran away to France, where he had a son, who was therefore considered by British Catholics as the rightful ruler of Britain). The Immaculate Order was just a minor religion at the beginning of the Shogunate, but by the end was widespread. The succession law could have imposed some religious test and defranchised others who could have been Shogun, but followed a different religion.<br /> <br /> This of course is ignoring all the craziness that could happen with magic. If the Shogun uses Neomah to have a kid with her lesbian lover, is it legitimate, or considered stained with Infernalism? What about stones of gender transformation? What if the Shogun marries a god and their first-born heir is some sort of wacky inhuman monster? What if the heir's mother turns out to be a Lunar spy? What if everyone's sure there definitely was an heir, but no one can remember his or her name, or knows where they've gone, as he's now languishing in a Sidereal prison?<br /> <br /> So, whatever the system was, I doubt it was simple.<br /> <br /> <br /> *This raises the question of exactly how many Shoguns there were. It's entirely possible there were, say, 3. Even 2 (as we discussed in another thread, it's not clear how long the Shogunate was because different times are given in different books). I assume that they were always getting murdered or overthrown though, so there was more 10 or 20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-26-2015, 05:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T02:19:02-07:00","id":492446,"title":"","content":"Oh, I should add to the &quot;what if&quot; questions above, it may be that there was, originally, no succession law to cover these things.<br /> <br /> When Henry I died, there was no clear succession, because he only had 1 daughter, and it just wasn't clear whether girls could inherit or not. There was no formal inheritance law to explain, the system of Agnatic-Cognatic Primogeniture (the oldest son inherits, unless there are no sons, in which case the oldest daughter inherits) was only formally written later.<br /> That wouldn't apply to the Shogunate, but it could be that originally the family was so pure-bred that they always Exalted, and then one day the heir wasn't an Exalt, and no-one knew what to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T08:55:57-07:00","id":492615,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you're right, it would likely have been very complicated.<br /> I reread my post and it looks like I'm saying Raikuru definitely isn't the heir. I only meant that nobody knows. He has Breeding 5 though, so he has a decent claim to good ancestry at least!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T01:28:49-07:00","id":493373,"title":"","content":"I would say that while there were some legal speculators who would devise an enormous, convoluted diversity of implications and applications for succession in the Shogunate, it generally tended to be academic. In practice, every child (and sibling and parent's sibling and distant cousin) of the shogun believed themselves to be the rightful heir, and the one who was correct was invariably the one with the most military support. There was never any strictly codified standard of succession, because no shogun wanted to deal with the fallout.<br /> <br /> Daimyos would vary between also putting their support behind potential candidates, merely trying to deprive support to candidates they specifically didn't want, and taking the opportunities represented by breakdowns in central authority to expand their own powers and holdings.<br /> <br /> Using sorcery and demon magic to mess around with your children is something I see as having relatively little legal rumination to it, on the grounds of taboo, and the fact that most of them aren't messing around with that stuff anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T01:58:07-07:00","id":493384,"title":"","content":"It might not have much legal weight, but I could definitely see a younger daughter rousing support for her claim among the pious by pointing out that the elder daughter was a creation of foul witchcraft.<br /> <br /> It probably didn't happen all that much... but I'm sure, with all the dramatic shenanigans of Dragonblood, something like that happened at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}